      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's helpful. i noticed you leaned quite heavily into the \"vibrant/energetic\" look for the nigerian segment and the \"geometric/jewel tone\" look for the middle eastern segment. \n\njust thinking out loud here, but do you think we should be careful not to make those versions look too \"traditional\" or \"ethnic\"? i don't want the app to look like a travel app or something \"folksy\" for them. for the western users like liam, you suggested a \"sophisticated/functional\" look—is there a reason we wouldn't want to use that same \"sophisticated\" standard for the others, or do they inherently require a more colorful/patterned aesthetic to feel \"right\" to them?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
